      "seed": 715537667,
      "version": 27,
      "versionNonce": 145789635,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784036390518,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Rate Limiter\nA rate limiter controls how many requests a client can make within a specific timeframe. It acts like a traffic controller for your API\nRate limiters prevent abuse, protect your servers from being overwhelmed by bursts of traffic, and ensure fair usage across all users.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Rate Limiter\nA rate limiter controls how many requests a client can make within a specific timeframe. It acts like a traffic controller for your API\nRate limiters prevent abuse, protect your servers from being overwhelmed by bursts of traffic, and ensure fair usage across all users.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "29uqUs0ypib8PFl9FyxFH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -26541.900708979785,
      "y": -4428.535366530659,
      "width": 688.5794677734375,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1821153805,
      "version": 455,
      "versionNonce": 1565168717,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784036646513,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements(rate limiter for social media app)\n- identify users by id, IP or API key\n- limit requests based on configurable rules(eg. 100 requests/min/user)\n- return proper error headers and status codes\n\n------- Out of Scope ------\n- complex querying on rate limiting\n- analytics on rate limiting\n- Long-term persistence of rate limiting data",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements(rate limiter for social media app)\n- identify users by id, IP or API key\n- limit requests based on configurable rules(eg. 100 requests/min/user)\n- return proper error headers and status codes\n\n------- Out of Scope ------\n- complex querying on rate limiting\n- analytics on rate limiting\n- Long-term persistence of rate limiting data",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pvXDmcCnv-WCFd0tbODe1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -26533.097620856453,
      "y": -4145.736160569211,
      "width": 419.79974365234375,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1167457763,
      "version": 166,
      "versionNonce": 777319427,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784036710359,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Non-functional Requirements\n- low latency check < 10ms\n- availability >> consistency\n- scale to 1M req/sec across 100M DAU    ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Non-functional Requirements\n- low latency check < 10ms\n- availability >> consistency\n- scale to 1M req/sec across 100M DAU    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "i2bv3QNt-EiVd9o35xd1n",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -26527.595690779388,
      "y": -3959.7709239642186,
      "width": 1325.9990234375,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1654777037,
      "version": 388,
      "versionNonce": 1518573,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784037072803,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Core Entities\n- Rules (stores rate limiting policies(requests per time window) for different scenarios, eg. authenticated users get 1000 req/hour etc.)\n- Clients (users identified by their userId, IP or API key or a combination of some or all)\n- Requests (incoming API request that needs to be evaluated against rate limiting rules)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Core Entities\n- Rules (stores rate limiting policies(requests per time window) for different scenarios, eg. authenticated users get 1000 req/hour etc.)\n- Clients (users identified by their userId, IP or API key or a combination of some or all)\n- Requests (incoming API request that needs to be evaluated against rate limiting rules)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "R4yEynezCt6sCqB64BKX5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -26524.294532733147,
      "y": -3808.880491600546,
      "width": 949.4193725585938,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1325714499,
      "version": 210,
      "versionNonce": 1730008995,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784037193139,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "System Interface\n- Its not a customer facing request/design so REST not applicable, internal system call(gRPC)\n\nisRequestAllowed(clientId, ruleId) -> { passes: boolean, remaining: number, resetTime: timestamp }\n\ncan also provide response headers like X-RateLimit-Remaining and X-RateLimit-Reset",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "System Interface\n- Its not a customer facing request/design so REST not applicable, internal system call(gRPC)\n\nisRequestAllowed(clientId, ruleId) -> { passes: boolean, remaining: number, resetTime: timestamp }\n\ncan also provide response headers like X-RateLimit-Remaining and X-RateLimit-Reset",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "tKNb_wGPpsG_Dne1mLeUZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -27628.049983700843,
      "y": -3583.6516128087615,
      "width": 2090.098388671875,
      "height": 700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 543125027,
      "version": 2325,
      "versionNonce": 2102841773,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784057351022,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Notes\n\nWhere to place the rate limiter?\n- The placement of the rate limiter is of high architectural significance\n\n1. Bad Solution : In-Process\n- Rate limiter lives inside the microservices itself\n- When request comes in server checks in local memory counter and makes a decision, very fast as no external network call needed, everything is in memory\nProblem : Each server knows about its own traffic, doesn't know the global picture of all servers\nUsers keeps on hitting different servers and never hit rate limiting, only works with single application server\n\n\n2. Good Solution : Dedicated Server\n- A common rate limiter is on a dedicated server i.e. its becomes its own microservice that servers reach out before responding to the request\n- Allows you to control rate limiting rules more as you have all the data of servers and users and rules, say allowing extra requests on black friday or allow more to premium user etc.\nProblems: High latency, additional hop before response, another point of failure introduced\nIf rate limiting service goes down decide\n    - Fail Open : allow all requests through, risking overload\n    - Fail Close : reject all requests, essentially taking your API offline\nneither is great.\n- And why to allow a request to reach microservice and then reject it, should be done before at API gateway layer.\n\n\n3. Great Solution : API Gateway/LB\n- Production rate limiter are integrated to gateway or LB, every request hits limiter first then our server if allowed\n- If failed returns HTTP status 429 (Too many Requests)\nProblems : rate limiter when placed at this layer only has access to info available in HTTP request, can't see deeper business logic, tough to implement rules like extra for premium user, unless that's encoded in JWT\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Notes\n\nWhere to place the rate limiter?\n- The placement of the rate limiter is of high architectural significance\n\n1. Bad Solution : In-Process\n- Rate limiter lives inside the microservices itself\n- When request comes in server checks in local memory counter and makes a decision, very fast as no external network call needed, everything is in memory\nProblem : Each server knows about its own traffic, doesn't know the global picture of all servers\nUsers keeps on hitting different servers and never hit rate limiting, only works with single application server\n\n\n2. Good Solution : Dedicated Server\n- A common rate limiter is on a dedicated server i.e. its becomes its own microservice that servers reach out before responding to the request\n- Allows you to control rate limiting rules more as you have all the data of servers and users and rules, say allowing extra requests on black friday or allow more to premium user etc.\nProblems: High latency, additional hop before response, another point of failure introduced\nIf rate limiting service goes down decide\n    - Fail Open : allow all requests through, risking overload\n    - Fail Close : reject all requests, essentially taking your API offline\nneither is great.\n- And why to allow a request to reach microservice and then reject it, should be done before at API gateway layer.\n\n\n3. Great Solution : API Gateway/LB\n- Production rate limiter are integrated to gateway or LB, every request hits limiter first then our server if allowed\n- If failed returns HTTP status 429 (Too many Requests)\nProblems : rate limiter when placed at this layer only has access to info available in HTTP request, can't see deeper business logic, tough to implement rules like extra for premium user, unless that's encoded in JWT\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ONAt_94WlFGq0hW1ItYb7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -27620.5100542533,
      "y": -2817.371041616696,
      "width": 1502.038818359375,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 125056205,
      "version": 606,
      "versionNonce": 639022509,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784057617716,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How to identify clients?\n- Use userID as an unique identifier for authenticated APIs, allowing logged in user their own rate limit allocation, present in Auth header as a JWT\n- Use IP for public APIs when we don't have user accounts, careful for users behind NATs and corporate firewalls. IP present in X-Forwarded-For header\n- Use API key for developer APIs, present in X-API-Key header\n\n- In practice, use combination per user say 1000 req/h, per IP say 100 req/min, global limits 50k req/sec total",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How to identify clients?\n- Use userID as an unique identifier for authenticated APIs, allowing logged in user their own rate limit allocation, present in Auth header as a JWT\n- Use IP for public APIs when we don't have user accounts, careful for users behind NATs and corporate firewalls. IP present in X-Forwarded-For header\n- Use API key for developer APIs, present in X-API-Key header\n\n- In practice, use combination per user say 1000 req/h, per IP say 100 req/min, global limits 50k req/sec total",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
