      "seed": 238007107,
      "version": 1248,
      "versionNonce": 600959619,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784058627821,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- keep track of individual TS for each user, when new request arrives, remove all TS older than your window(older than 1 min ago)\n- Then check if remaining count exceeds your limit.\n- So, maintain a DS to store TS equal to your global limit or say per user limit, if say 100 requests accumulated in 1 min window, don't accept the 101th request until the previous minute requests are dropped dynamically.\nProblem : High memory usage, stores all TS for all users all request, computational overhead for scanning through TS and adding/removing them.\n\n\n\n3. Sliding Window Counter\n- Clever Hybrid to approximate sliding windows using fixed windows with some math\n- Maintain counter for current window and previous window, when new request comes in estimate how many requests the user \"should have\" made in a true sliding window by weighing the previous and current windows based on how far you are into the current window.\n- say if 30 through the current minute you count 70% of previous minute's requests + 100% of the current minute requests\n- Just two counters per client\nProblem : its approximation that traffic is even\n\n\n4. Token Bucket",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- keep track of individual TS for each user, when new request arrives, remove all TS older than your window(older than 1 min ago)\n- Then check if remaining count exceeds your limit.\n- So, maintain a DS to store TS equal to your global limit or say per user limit, if say 100 requests accumulated in 1 min window, don't accept the 101th request until the previous minute requests are dropped dynamically.\nProblem : High memory usage, stores all TS for all users all request, computational overhead for scanning through TS and adding/removing them.\n\n\n\n3. Sliding Window Counter\n- Clever Hybrid to approximate sliding windows using fixed windows with some math\n- Maintain counter for current window and previous window, when new request comes in estimate how many requests the user \"should have\" made in a true sliding window by weighing the previous and current windows based on how far you are into the current window.\n- say if 30 through the current minute you count 70% of previous minute's requests + 100% of the current minute requests\n- Just two counters per client\nProblem : its approximation that traffic is even\n\n\n4. Token Bucket",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
